In article <16C84B346.CHBRIN5@nyx.uni-konstanz.de>, CHBRIN5@nyx.uni-konstanz.de
(Kai Hortmann) says:
>
>3) I ate a water nymph corpse and teleported at random times to random places.
>   When I tried to buy something in a shop, I teleported out accidentaly and
>   had the shopkeeper and kops after me. Is there a way to pay your debt
>   afterwards and make the shopkeeper peaceful again?

The (p)ay command still works, but you have to be next to the shopkeeper.
You don't even have to be in the shop at the time.  I remember a game,
where I was roaming the lighting shop, picked up 2-3 candles (with
full intention to buy them) and then randomly teleported out.
After wading through a dozen Kops or so, I finally found the shopkeeper.
I paid my bill (15-30 gold), and that was that.  The shopkeeper was
happy, and he called off all the Kops (what few were still alive.)
I had no further run-ins with the law on that level.  Didn't even
have to pay funeral expenses.
>
>4) How does one train a pet? Or is it just growing stronger with time and
>   doesn't learn any new tricks? I'd like to be able to send my dog somewhere.

I've never seen any New tricks.  The bigger pets just start picking
up bigger things (like plate mail and large boxes).  As far as
training, I don't do anything particularly special:

Stand in the doorway (make the shopkeeper think you're going to
step inside any moment.  Then think at your pet:  I'm not going
to let you out of this room unless you're carrying something!
Since pets randomly pick things up and drop them, it just takes
a bit of patience.

Also, since they often seem to like to be Near me, I have to
modify my tactic when the front half of the shop empties out.
I walk over to the far side from the door -- (here kitty kitty)
Eventually they come by, and pick a few things up.  I can't
always get them to carry those items clear out of the shop,
but at least when I know which are uncursed, I can carry them
towards the front door myself, and have my pet do the rest.

Oh, by the way, about your pet getting stronger:
Every time it kills something its maximum hitpoints increase
(something like 1+monster level).  Every eight hit-points
it gains a level.  The pet maxes out at Level 9 with 72 hitpoints.
Beyond that point, its kills do nothing but steal your XP
and your food supply.

